<!--
  A single-file, dependency-free canvas plate of a B-DNA double helix.

  Geometry   : both backbones are sampled from one helix parametric —
               angle θ = (rot + y·twist)·(1 − melt), strand B sits at θ + π,
               so each base-pair rung is an exact horizontal chord through the axis.
               Mild x-only perspective + depth-sorted painter's algorithm gives the
               over/under weave where the strands cross.
  Rendering  : sea-glass teal vs. warm sand for the antiparallel strands; rung strokes
               are gradients between the two backbone colors, alternating weak/strong
               (A–T · two H-bonds / G–C · three). Film grain, studio lift, plate falloff.
  Interaction: drag to spin (with inertia), wheel / pinch to zoom, arrow keys to nudge —
               and the signature one: brush the molecule to locally denature it
